  "limitations": "This does not complete MR-10 or the 17-package goal. Bindings alone are not live-quorum join authorization. Native fresh-member authorization, peer/S3 seeding, permanent claim reconciliation and the complete native recovery fault matrix remain. Learner-first/catch-up guards are tested at the serialized Raft adapter; no automatic membership controller or native replacement lifecycle is qualified. One archive and some snapshot fixtures deliberately use trusted mechanical storage to inject invalid state; ordinary native catalog admission remains separate. The marker-1 protocol identity cellar-raft-ltx-1/members-1 refuses earlier namespace roots; there is no compatibility reader or migration. A fresh experimental namespace/prefix and local state are required. Snapshot completion capacity is now eight slots/128 KiB with a 16-KiB reservation per snapshot. Object storage is in-memory; the 64-MiB boundary is a mechanically seeded physical image, not a 64-MiB SDK command. Current Node coverage is the affected Raft lifecycle case; the separate 304-case evidence retains its earlier 88-Node source qualification and is not rerun or claimed at this source. No physical S3, power loss, zones, production performance/capacity, larger scale, federation or complete release qualification is claimed. Seven ignored child entry points are invoked by owning parents and excluded. Existing vendored warnings remain visible.",
